    <!-- The API itself is plain HTTP with no domain yet (see FullTime.Api/Program.cs's own comment
         on this) — regular API calls already work today, likely because .NET's default HTTP stack
         on iOS doesn't enforce ATS the same way SignalR.Client's connection does internally (same
         asymmetry confirmed on Android: SignalR failed with a cleartext block that the app's own
         HttpClient never hit). Added pre-emptively so the SignalR live-score push doesn't silently
         fail the same way on a real iPhone. -->
    <key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
    <dict>
        <key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>
    <!-- Google's published TEST AdMob app ID - temporarily swapped back in while real ads aren't
         filling yet. Swap back to the real ID (see git history) once that's sorted. -->
    <key>GADApplicationIdentifier</key>
    <string>ca-app-pub-3940256099942544~1458002511</string>
    <key>GADIsAdManagerApp</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- Confirmed missing on a real ad-hoc build: no ads ever showed. Both of these are required by
         AdMob's iOS setup docs, not optional extras - without NSUserTrackingUsageDescription the app
         never even asks for tracking permission (AppDelegate.OnActivated requests it), and without
         SKAdNetworkItems, ad networks report "required SKAdNetwork identifier(s) missing" and can
         refuse to fill at all rather than just attributing less accurately. -->
